; Tutorial_1_User_Interface.inix -- user interface

[about]
Title=1 - User Interface
Intro=The urlFido dialog: its fields and boxes, their underlined letters, and the keys that work anywhere in it, each shown as the reader speaks it.
Setup=urlFido installed; the dialog open with Alt+Control+U.
Homework=Open the dialog, move to File extensions with its letter, and press Shift+F1 to hear its tip.

[step]

Say=One want: to move around the urlFido dialog quickly, knowing what every field and box does before the first download.
Key=

[step]

Say=I press the desktop key. The dialog opens on its first field.
Key=Alt+Control+U
Hear=urlFido dialog
Hear=Source urls edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Source urls names the pages to fetch from: one address, several separated by spaces, or the path of a text file listing them. Its letter is S.
Key=

[step]

Say=Tab moves to the next control, a button that picks such a file.
Key=Tab
Hear=Browse source button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt with an underlined letter jumps to a control. File extensions is E.
Key=Alt+E
Hear=File extensions edit, docx pdf zip
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=It holds the kinds of file to fetch, separated by spaces or commas. Walk four explains its patterns.
Key=

[step]

Say=Output directory, O, is the parent folder; each page gets a folder of its own inside it. Choose output, C, picks it instead of typing.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Output directory edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Then the boxes. Test fetch, T, does everything but download, and reports what it would have done.
Key=Alt+T
Hear=Test fetch check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Force overwrite, F, replaces files already there; without it, a second copy of a file is saved with a number added to its name.
Key=Alt+F
Hear=Force overwrite check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Authenticate credentials, A, pauses at each new site so you can sign in; Main profile, M, uses your everyday Edge and its saved sign ins.
Key=Alt+A
Hear=Authenticate credentials check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Invisible browser, I, runs Edge with no window.
Key=Alt+I
Hear=Invisible browser check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=View output, V, opens the folder at the end; Log session, L, keeps a log; Use configuration, U, remembers your choices.
Key=Alt+V
Hear=View output check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Space checks a box, and Space again clears it.
Key=Space
Hear=checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Space.
Key=Space
Hear=not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus F1 says the tip for the control you are on.
Key=Shift+F1
Hear=View output: open the output folder when the run is done
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=F1 shows Help, every control and every key.
Key=F1
Hear=urlFido Help dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes Help and returns to the same place.
Key=Escape
Hear=View output check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter starts the run from any field, and Control plus Enter from any control. Escape closes the dialog without fetching.
Key=Tab
Hear=Use configuration check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Default settings, D, clears every field and box and deletes the saved configuration, for starting fresh.
Key=Alt+D
Hear=Default settings button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The text fields remember earlier answers: Up Arrow in Source urls brings back the pages fetched before.
Key=Up Arrow
Hear=https colon slash slash www dot itic dot org slash policy slash accessibility slash vpat
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Text fields also take the editing keys used across Homer programs, which the guide lists in full.
Key=

[step]

Say=Command-line values and the dialog share letters: each short option is the same letter as its control's access key, so learning one teaches the other.
Key=Alt+E
Hear=File extensions edit, docx pdf zip
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=That is the dialog: pages, kinds of file, a folder, seven boxes, and a key for each. The next walk installs urlFido.
Key=
